  "solution": {
    "text": "The wall acts like a rigid boundary and reflects this wave and sends it back towards the open end. At the open an antinode is formed and a node is formed at the wall. The distance between antinode and node is<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Therefore, if v be the frequency of note emitted then<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10233;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mn>600</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br /><br />Maximum amplitude is obtained at a distance<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>"
  }
}